Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE).

HALean is a translation into Lean 4 of parts of Home Assistant Core and of
libraries it uses. Those parts are derivative works of the upstream code; the
Lean files say which upstream functions they translate ("Translated from ..."),
and manifest.yaml maps each upstream Python function to its Lean version. The
translations are changed from the original: they are rewritten in another
language and only model a subset of the original behaviour.

Upstream works, their licenses and where the license texts are:

* Home Assistant Core 2026.10.4 (https://github.com/home-assistant/core)
  Copyright the Home Assistant authors.
  Apache License 2.0: LICENSES/home-assistant-core.Apache-2.0.md

* probatio 0.13.0, Home Assistant's validation library
  (https://pypi.org/project/probatio/)
  Copyright (c) 2026 Franck Nijhof. MIT License: LICENSES/probatio.MIT.txt

* Jinja2 3.1.6, the template engine Home Assistant uses
  (https://github.com/pallets/jinja)
  Copyright 2007 Pallets. BSD 3-Clause License: LICENSES/jinja2.BSD-3-Clause.txt

* astral 2.2, the solar calculator Home Assistant uses
  (https://github.com/sffjunkie/astral)
  Apache License 2.0: LICENSES/astral.Apache-2.0.txt

* python-slugify 9.1.2, behind homeassistant.util.slugify
